# Keys typed ahead with the Enter before them (docs/repl.md, While a
# declaration runs): two entries written at once, as a terminal gives a
# REPL that was busy what was typed meanwhile, reach the editor in one
# read. The second is the editor's at the next prompt and runs; it was
# lost when the editor dropped what a read held after the end of a line
# (tests/lib/terminal/ahead.sml). Read by bin/rune-terminal raw, which
# writes the two in one write.
until \x1b\[\?2004h.*\x1b\]133;A\x1b\\ 20
write 1;\r2;\r
until val.*it.* = 1 : int.*\x1b\]133;D;0\x1b\\.*val.*it.* = 2 : int.*\x1b\]133;D;0\x1b\\ 20
write \x04
quiet 300
